        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: برآورد کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "برآورد کردن (barâvard kardan) — \"to estimate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پلیس تعداد مردم را ده هزار نفر برآورد کرد. Polis te'dâd-e mardom râ dah hezâr nafar barâvard kard. The police estimated the crowd at ten thousand people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "barâvard \"an estimate\" is built on bar \"up\" and âvard, from âvardan \"to bring\": to bring up a figure. Present barâvard mikonad."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "barâvard joins bar \"up, on\" and âvard, the past stem of âvardan \"to bring\", both native Persian; kardan \"to do\" is inherited too. EtymDB lists no entry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
