          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تاکید کردن (ta'kid kardan) — \"to stress, to emphasise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پزشک تاکید کرد که بیمار باید استراحت کند. Pezeshk ta'kid kard ke bimâr bâyad esterâhat konad. The doctor stressed that the patient had to rest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With bar or a ke clause: bar in nokte ta'kid kard. Careful print adds a hamza sign. Present ta'kid mikonad."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ta'kid is borrowed from Arabic ta'kīd, \"emphasis, confirmation\" (EtymDB lists the Arabic word). kardan \"to do\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
